// The eight-wide tree over triangles: what Embree's BVH8 and FCPW's
// eight-wide Mbvh both are, before either gives it bytes. An interior node
// holds eight children as one array with one box annotation over them,
// `AABB(lo, hi) on children` -- the node bounds its children, not itself,
// as Embree's AABBNode and FCPW's MbvhNode both do -- so a traversal tests
// the eight at the node (Lower/Trees.cpp, from_children), which a schedule
// vectorizes into one eight-wide test. A leaf holds a run of triangles.
//
// The bytes are a layout's: schedules/layouts/embree8.bonsai (Embree's
// AABBNode<8> rows and Triangle4 blocks in one arena, reached by address),
// schedules/layouts/fcpw8w16.bonsai and fcpw8w8.bonsai (FCPW's MbvhNode
// rows of eight and packets of sixteen or eight, reached by index). Each
// imports this file; the schedules import a layout.

schedule {
    tree[[Triangle]] BVH8 =
    | Interior(children : array[BVH8, 8], lo hi : vector[vec3f, 8])
        with AABB(lo, hi) on children
    | Leaf(data : array[Triangle]) with data = data;

    triangles : BVH8;
}
